A file whose endings are mostly CRLF says so in its header, since the rendered lines cannot show a
`\r`. The second call is the control: an LF file's header has no such segment.

```console
$ lets show win.txt
── win.txt  (1-2 of 2) · crlf
1 	one
2 	two
── showed 1 target · 2 lines

$ lets show unix.txt
── unix.txt  (1-2 of 2)
1 	one
2 	two
── showed 1 target · 2 lines

```
